      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It is very weird that the height of the Quick Menu's profile page depends on the length of the user's bio.\n\nMalicious users would just use this to their advantage, making their bio as long as possible to ensure that the block/kick/ban buttons are as far down the page as possible, just to throw off muscle memory.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-07-26T04:19:12.639Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Showing and hiding avatars is a very important setting that should always be front and center when you click on someone, as it is something that pretty much all of us do when we have safety settings on and want to see other people's avatars or when we have to hide them quickly when they are lagging our game. It would really benefit to have the buttons in the same place at all times and not have it jump around depending on how long someone's bio is. The current position of it messes with people's muscle memory and adds an extra point of friction to a feature that people use in pretty much every instance they join, especially quest/mobile users as they always need to show people's avatars regardless of their safety settings.",
